# Cross-origin isolation.
#
# `performance.measureUserAgentSpecificMemory()` is the only API that can see an
# ImageBitmap, a GPU-backed canvas or a detached buffer — `performance.memory`
# reports the JS heap and would say 15MB while a quarter of a gigabyte of pixels
# is resident. It refuses to run without these two headers.
#
# This is what settled the hosting question left open since the branch-protection
# 403: GitHub Pages cannot set response headers, so it cannot be measured there.
# Cloudflare Pages and Netlify both read this file and both deploy from a private
# repository.
#
# Safe here because the application loads nothing cross-origin: no CDN, no fonts,
# no analytics. Images are opened from the user's disk and never fetched.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
